======================================================
ICMP
======================================================
“ICMP is a Layer 3 protocol used for network diagnostics and error reporting, commonly used by ping and traceroute.”


| Symptom        | ICMP Result             |
| -------------- | ----------------------- |
| Host down      | No echo reply           |
| Firewall block | Request sent, no reply  |
| TTL expired    | Time Exceeded           |
| Route missing  | Destination unreachable |


======================================================
What is ping?
======================================================
ping is a network diagnostic command used to test reachability between two hosts.
Protocol: ICMP
OSI Layer: Layer 3 (Network layer)
Purpose: Check if a host is alive + measure latency

======================================================
How ping works (behind the scenes)
======================================================
Your system sends an ICMP Echo Request
Target replies with ICMP Echo Reply
ping measures round-trip time (RTT)
📌 No ports involved (unlike TCP/UDP)


======================================================
Basic ping command
======================================================
ping google.com
-----------------------------
Typical output:
-----------------------------
64 bytes from 142.250.190.14: icmp_seq=1 ttl=118 time=22.4 ms

-----------------------------
How to read this line
-----------------------------
64 bytes → payload size
icmp_seq=1 → sequence number
ttl=118 → hops left
time=22.4 ms → latency


======================================================
When ping fails – what it means
======================================================
| Output                         | Meaning                     |
| ------------------------------ | --------------------------- |
| `Request timeout`              | Host unreachable / firewall |
| `Destination Host Unreachable` | Routing issue               |
| `100% packet loss`             | Host down or ICMP blocked   |
| Ping works, app fails          | Layer 4/7 issue             |


======================================================
Ping in AWS / Cloud 
======================================================
EC2 Security Groups may block ICMP
NACLs may block ICMP
Load balancers often don’t reply to ping
📌 Ping failing ≠ instance down

Note:
ping uses ICMP
ICMP has no ports
Ports belong to TCP/UDP (Layer 4)
